    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1938" root="بد" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدِيدٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِدٌّ</span>, in three places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A saddlebag;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُرْجٌ</span>: (K:) [and] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدِيدَانِ</span> <i>a pair of
saddle-bags;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُرْجَانِ</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِدَادٌ</span>,
in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  Also <i>A wide</i> [<i>desert such as is
termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفَازَة</span>: (S, K:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَاةٌ بَدِيدٌ</span> [<i>a desert,</i> or
<i>waterless desert,</i>] <i>in which is no one.</i> (T, L. [In
a copy of the former written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدْ بَدٌ</span>.])

